# Deny by default; the shipping set is the un-ignored list below.
#
# GATE 0.3. `wrangler.jsonc` is the canonical config and its `assets.directory` is this
# directory, which has grown to 97 MB across 318 walked entries. The full tree does not upload:
# a 48 MB attempt failed with a connectivity error after ~49 s, which is why
# `scripts/stage-edge-assets.sh` and `experiments/wrangler/wrangler.edge*.jsonc` existed
# at all. This file replaces that staging step: the subset is declared next to the assets
# instead of copied into a parallel directory served by a parallel config, so there is one
# config, one directory, and no build step to forget before a deploy.
#
# It is ALSO a disclosure fix. Workers assets are served publicly and take precedence over
# the Worker, so `assets.directory: ./assets` published the whole site database at
# /drupal/site.sqlite and every measurement fixture alongside it.
#
# THE SHIPPING SET IS DERIVED FROM THE CANONICAL VARS, not from what looks useful:
#   LAZY_MOUNT=1        -> mountDrupalLazy() reads drupal-pf/core.pf.{json,bin}
#                          (@drupflare/cartridge/fs)
#   MIGRATE_ENGINE unset -> migrateEngine() defaults to 'sql' in src/site-do.ts, so `database`
#                          is false and NOTHING fetches site.sqlite; the shipping binary carries
#                          no pdo_sqlite to open it with either
#   the JS engine replays drupal-sql/ (assetChunkLoader, src/db/migrate-sql.ts:508)
#   mountDriver() reads driver.json (@drupflare/cartridge/fs)
#   the free-tier prefill reads prefill.json (the /__migrate handler in src/site-do.ts)
#
# So changing LAZY_MOUNT, MIGRATE_ENGINE or SITE_DB_PREFIX in a deploying config means
# changing this file too, and `tests/unit/runtime/assets-ignore.spec.ts` is what fails when
# the two disagree.
/*

!/driver.json
!/prefill.json

# the Drupal static tree, which the BROWSER fetches at /core/**. Every pack skips these extensions
# because PHP never opens them, and nothing serves a file out of the MEMFS over HTTP -- so the asset
# layer is the only thing that can answer them. scripts/pack-static.ts writes it
!/core/
!/modules/

# the lazy mount's per-file pack; prefix is fixed at drupal-pf in @drupflare/cartridge/fs
!/drupal-pf/
/drupal-pf/*
!/drupal-pf/core.pf.json
!/drupal-pf/core.pf.bin

# the migration chunks the JS engine replays: manifest.json plus NNNN.json
!/drupal-sql/
